      "claim": "In a DFS tree of a connected undirected graph, any edge not in the tree is a back edge connecting a vertex to one of its ancestors.",
      "evidence": "Standard property of DFS in undirected graphs: no cross edges exist. If an edge connected two nodes not in an ancestor-descendant relationship, it would be a cross edge, which is impossible because the first node visited would have discovered the second as a child or the second would have been on the recursion stack.",
