      "claim": "Given pre(u) < pre(v) for the non-tree edge (u, v), u must be an ancestor of v in T.",
      "evidence": "Since (u, v) is a back edge, one endpoint is an ancestor of the other. In a preorder traversal, ancestors are visited before descendants. Therefore, the node with the smaller preorder number (u) is the ancestor, and the node with the larger preorder number (v) is the descendant.",
