      "evidence": "The Lowest Common Ancestor (LCA) of two nodes is the deepest node that is an ancestor of both. Since u is an ancestor of v (Step 2), u is a common ancestor. No child of u can be an ancestor of u itself, so u is the deepest common ancestor. Thus, LCA(u, v) = u.",
